## Quick Reference

Rows are one paper each. `Slug` is a stable kebab-case identifier used as the foreign-key anchor into PAPER_SUMMARIES.md. `Key Contribution` is a ≤50-word thesis; full summary and numerical findings live in PAPER_SUMMARIES.md. The table is generated by `paper_index.py index` from each entry's `Focus` / `One-liner` (/ `Index label`) fields, in section order — edit the entry, not the row. Entries still missing those fields have no row yet. See the `add-paper` skill for the slug rules and PAPER_RELATED.md for the reverse index of `Related` links.

